@startuml raditrack_activity_test_data_verification
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #334155

title RADiTrack — Activity Diagram: Verifying Calculations with the Validation Dataset

' ==============================================================================
' SWIMLANES
' ==============================================================================

|Administrator|
start
:Open RIS Simulator →\n**Load 100-exam test dataset**;
:Confirm;

|RADiTrack|
:Turn the 100 test exams' relative dates\n(today / week start / month start)\ninto real timestamps;
if (Any test exam invalid\n(e.g. loaded before 00:30)?) then (yes)
  :Show the problem; nothing changes;
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (Real data already backed up?) then (no)
  :Back up real exams and reports\n(backup tables);
else (yes)
endif
:In one transaction: replace exams\nwith the test dataset;
:Show "TEST DATA ACTIVE" banner\non every staff screen;

|Administrator|
fork
  :Open the test workbook in Excel;
  :Read the Expected sheets\n(recalculated from TODAY());
  :Compare with the dashboard;
fork again
  :Run **npm run test-data:verify**;

  |RADiTrack|
  :Recompute expected values from\nraw timestamps (reference calculator);
  :Call the same functions the dashboard\nand PDF report use;
  :Write Expected vs RADiTrack with\nPASS/FAIL per value to the\nVerification sheet;

  |Administrator|
  :Review the verification report;
end fork

if (All values match?) then (yes)
  :Keep the report as evidence;
else (no)
  :Investigate the failing values;
endif
:Open RIS Simulator →\n**Restore real data**;

|RADiTrack|
:In one transaction: remove test data,\nrestore exams and reports from backup,\ndrop backup tables;
:Hide the test-data banner;
stop

@enduml
